---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const updated = new Date("2026-10-27");
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site stores on your device, what it does not do, and who to contact."
>
  <h1
    class="font-display font-extrabold tracking-tight text-3xl sm:text-4xl leading-tight"
  >
    Privacy
  </h1>
  <p class="font-mono text-xs text-muted mt-3">
    Last updated <time datetime={updated.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}
      >{updated.toLocaleDateString("en-GB", { year: "numeric", month: "long", day: "numeric" })}</time
    >
  </p>

  <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none font-serif mt-8">
    <p>
      This is a personal, static website. It has no accounts, no forms, no
      comments and no advertising. Here is everything it does with your data.
    </p>

    <h2>No cookies, no tracking</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics. It loads no scripts,
      fonts, images or embeds from third-party services, so no other company
      learns that you visited. There is no consent banner because there is
      nothing to consent to.
    </p>

    <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      If you use the light/dark toggle in the header, your choice is saved in
      your browser's local storage under a single key named <code>theme</code>,
      so the site remembers it on your next visit. That value never leaves your
      browser and contains nothing that identifies you. Clearing your browser
      data removes it. If you never touch the toggle, nothing is stored and the
      site simply follows your operating system's colour scheme.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served by <a href="https://pages.github.com/">GitHub Pages</a>.
      As with any web host, GitHub may record your IP address and the pages you
      request in its server logs for security and operational purposes. I have
      no access to those logs. See the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
        >GitHub General Privacy Statement</a
      > for details.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Posts link to external sites such as GitHub, MDN or npm. Those links only
      load when you click them, and the destination site's own privacy terms
      apply from that point.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      This site is run by Ramón Miklus. If you email <a
        href="mailto:hello@ramonmiklus.com">hello@ramonmiklus.com</a
      >, I will use your address only to reply to you. If you have any question
      about this notice, write to the same address.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
